# Designer Workflow

The designer may not know the codebase or programming terms. Treat UI requests as product/design intent and translate them into safe implementation steps.

- Before changing UI, briefly explain the visual area you will touch and what will stay unchanged.
- Use simple product language in user-facing explanations; avoid requiring the designer to read code.
- Ask a clarifying question when the request is visually ambiguous, affects several screens, or changes behavior.
- After changes, summarize the result by screen/component and call out any non-visual change explicitly.
- Do not assume permission to change data flow, routes, API calls, permissions, validation, or auth for a design-only request.
- If the requested design needs new behavior or product logic, stop and explain what engineering decision is needed.
